<h1>How we handle your email</h1>

<p class="meta">
  Last updated <time datetime="{{ page.date | isoDate }}">{{ page.date | readableDate }}</time>
</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<p>
  If you subscribe, we store your email address. That is the only personal
  information we ask you for. We do not ask for your name, and there is no account to
  create.
</p>
<p>
  Our email provider{% if newsletter.provider %}, {{ newsletter.provider }},{% endif %}
  stores your address on our behalf and records the date you confirmed your
  subscription, plus whether recent emails to you bounced. That last part is how we
  stop sending to dead addresses.
</p>

<h2>What we do with it</h2>
<p>
  We use your address to send you our own writing. Nothing else. We do not sell it,
  rent it, trade it, or hand it to advertisers, and we do not send you other people's
  promotions.
</p>
<p>
  We never add an address that was not typed into our own form and then confirmed by
  clicking a link in an email. We do not buy lists, and we do not treat a business
  card, a reply, or a follow as permission.
</p>

<h2>Leaving</h2>
<p>
  Every email we send carries an unsubscribe link. One click removes you — no reply
  needed, no reason required, no “are you sure” page. If the link ever fails, email us
  and we will remove you by hand.
</p>

<h2>The rest of the site</h2>
<p>
  These pages are static files. There are no advertising or tracking cookies, no
  third-party scripts, and no web fonts, so reading here does not require you to
  trust anyone but us and our host.
</p>
